<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Albrecht von Wallenstein</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1583">1583</a>–1634</span> · <a href="/centuries/17th-century">17th century</a> · Also known as Albrecht von Waldstein</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Albrecht von Wallenstein was a Bohemian nobleman who raised and commanded the imperial armies in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/thirty-tyrants">the Thirty</a> Years' War. Rewarded with the duchies of Friedland, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/zagan">Sagan</a> and, in 1628, Mecklenburg, he became one of the most powerful men in the Empire. Suspected of treason, he was dismissed and then murdered at Eger in 1634 on the emperor's authority.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/albrecht-von-wallenstein.jpg" alt="Albrecht von Wallenstein" width="320" height="400" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Julius Schnorr von Carolsfeld · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Albrecht_von_Wallenstein.jpeg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
